<Base title="Privacy" description="How Listika uses hosting, Google AdSense and Google Analytics on its website.">
  <div class="wrap prose-layout"><div class="index-line"><span><a href="/">THE INDEX</a> / PRIVACY</span><span>LISTIKA</span></div><p class="eyebrow">SITE INFORMATION / 03</p><h1>Privacy.</h1><div class="prose"><p class="opening">This page explains the services currently included on Listika.</p><h2>Hosting</h2><p>Listika is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may process information such as visitors’ IP addresses as part of operating and securing the service. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p><h2>Google AdSense</h2><p>Listika includes Google AdSense code to connect the site to an advertising account. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve and measure advertising, subject to their settings and applicable consent requirements. You can read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites using its services</a> and manage settings in <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a>.</p><h2>Google Analytics</h2><p>Listika uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site. Google Analytics can use first-party cookies and collect information such as pages viewed, device and browser details, and approximate location to produce usage reports. Google processes this information to provide the service. Learn more about <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245">how Google Analytics collects and processes data</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites using its services</a>.</p><p>You can manage or delete cookies in your browser, and Google provides an <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a> for supported browsers.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Our lists link to other websites. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which we do not control.</p></div></div>
</Base>
